{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The book of the covenant.</b> The book in which he wrote the words of HaShem and the ordinances upon which the covenant would be struck, as it says above: וַיִּכְתֹּב בְּסֵפֶר — \"and he wrote in a book\" (Exodus 24:4)." "<b>And he read in the ears of the people.</b> So that they would know what they were taking upon themselves, so that they would not be as ones misled." "<b>We will do and we will hear.</b> We will do in order that we hear His voice as servants who attend upon the master not for the sake of receiving reward, as it says: עֹשֵׂי דְבָרוֹ לִשְׁמֹעַ בְּקוֹל דְבָרוֹ — \"doers of His word, to hear the voice of His word\" (Psalms 103:20)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:05.206469043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}